{{also|Amplitude}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|amplitudo||lang=la}}, from {{term|amplus||large|lang=la}}; see [[ample]] and [[-tude]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-amplitude.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[measure]] of something's [[size]], especially in terms of [[width]] or [[breadth]]; [[largeness]], [[magnitude]].
# {{mathematics}} The [[maximum]] [[absolute]] [[value]] of the [[vertical]] [[component]] of a [[curve]] or [[function]], especially one that is [[periodic]].
# {{physics}} The maximum absolute value of some quantity that [[varies]].

====Related terms====
* [[ample]]
* [[amplifiable]]
* [[amplification]]
* [[amplifier]]
* [[amplificatory]]
* [[amplify]]

